    {
      "id": "02-create",
      "instruction": "In Odoo 17 (already signed in as admin), go to the Sales app and create a new quotation. Set the Customer field to '{{runid}} Bench Customer' — this is an autocomplete dropdown, so you must type the name and actually pick the matching option from the dropdown that appears (not just type it). Then add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue using the product autocomplete dropdown (again, choose an option from the dropdown, don't just type), and set the quantity to 3. Let Odoo fill in the unit price automatically from the product's list price. Do NOT confirm the quotation yet — leave it as a draft quotation. Save the quotation and report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price Odoo filled in, (c) the Untaxed Amount the app computes, and (d) the quotation's reference/name (e.g. S00001). Note: the app long-polls so never wait for network idle — wait for concrete page state instead.",
